# bcm2711 (Raspberry Pi 4) drivers the arm64 defconfig leaves =m,
# forced built-in per the monolithic principle (no initramfs, AD-006;
# see boards/common/kernel/crag-net.fragment). Wifi (BRCMFMAC) stays a
# module on purpose: its firmware lives in the rootfs
# (firmware-linux-brcm-rpi), so a built-in driver would probe before
# /lib/firmware exists — the module loads post-mount instead.
#
# Ethernet (GENET) + the VL805 USB controller path (PCIe + xHCI +
# firmware-mediated reset) are what first-boot networking and a USB
# keyboard need.
CONFIG_BCMGENET=y
CONFIG_BROADCOM_PHY=y
CONFIG_PCIE_BRCMSTB=y
CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PCI=y
CONFIG_RESET_RASPBERRYPI=y
CONFIG_CLK_RASPBERRYPI=y
CONFIG_ARM_RASPBERRYPI_CPUFREQ=y
CONFIG_RASPBERRYPI_POWER=y
CONFIG_GPIO_RASPBERRYPI_EXP=y
# SD/MMC + mailbox/firmware are already =y via ARCH_BCM2835 defaults
# (MMC_BCM2835, MMC_SDHCI_IPROC, BCM2835_MBOX, RASPBERRYPI_FIRMWARE).
